+    A ``fallback_searchpath`` can be given to search additional directories
+    after the primary ``searchpath`` has been exhausted. This is a named
+    configuration convenience equivalent to one combined ordered path list.
+    If a primary file that supplied a cached template is deleted, its
+    ``uptodate`` callback becomes false and a later reload may resolve the
+    same name from a fallback path.
+
+    .. code-block:: python
+
+        loader = FileSystemLoader(
+            "/primary/templates",
+            fallback_searchpath="/fallback/templates",
+        )
+
     :param searchpath: A path, or list of paths, to the directory that
         contains the templates.
     :param encoding: Use this encoding to read the text from template
         files.
     :param followlinks: Follow symbolic links in the path.
+    :param fallback_searchpath: A path, or list of paths, to additional
+        directories to search after the primary searchpath is exhausted.
+        ``None`` or an empty sequence means no fallback paths.
 
     .. versionchanged:: 2.8
         Added the ``followlinks`` parameter.
